就 Jeff Layton 向 glibc 提交的 fcntl-linux.h 补丁（新增 F_OFD_GETLK32、F_OFD_SETLK32、 F_OFD_SETLKW32）而言，Mike Frysinger 提出应常设 64 与 32 两套宏、再按编译模式把 F_OFD_GETLK 等重定向 过去（"i think we should define *64 and *32 variants all the time, and then route the F_OFD_GETLK/etc... to them based on compile mode"），另指第一行后应留空行。被修改的注释位于 glibc 的 sysdeps/unix/sysv/linux/bits/fcntl-linux.h（非内核 UAPI 头），其中保留的表述为 "This means that they are inherited across fork or clone with CLONE_FILES like BSD (flock) locks, and they are only released automatically when the last reference to the the file description against which they were acquired is put."——即 BSD flock 式的 fork 可继承性被写入这份与内核 UAPI 语义对齐的文档文本。

